  "instance_name": "1992_Los_Angeles_Riots",
  "label": "1992 Los Angeles Riots",
  "description": "A series of civil disorders that erupted in Los Angeles, California, following the acquittal of police officers involved in the beating of Rodney King. The riots lasted for several days and resulted in widespread destruction, over 50 deaths, and thousands of injuries. The event is historically significant as a major expression of racial injustice and police brutality in the United States. The meme falsely claims that 'African American leaders' were 'organizing' the riots, which is a racist distortion of the legitimate anger and protest of the Black community.",
